ssage": "503 Service Unavailable: rollback", "attempts": 4, "runtime_actions": ["backoff_retry", "backoff_retry", "backoff_retry", "backoff_retry"], "failure_class": "semantic", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 27475, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012mv6pSaKEtpwatB9eEkgsS", "kind": "unavailable", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 30429, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J9PN8TKiVVmMSN1bfXCj4r", "tool": "deploy", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 35429, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J9PN8TKiVVmMSN1bfXCj4r", "tool": "deploy", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 35429, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J9PN8TKiVVmMSN1bfXCj4r", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 37048, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01At3Sf6PLd5RHfaoidzHhmL", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 37348, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01At3Sf6PLd5RHfaoidzHhmL", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 37348, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01At3Sf6PLd5RHfaoidzHhmL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 37348, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PnXzTsEo9amrMqXbUTBMrw", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 37648, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PnXzTsEo9amrMqXbUTBMrw", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 37648, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PnXzTsEo9amrMqXbUTBMrw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 41922, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_015cfSwdCSAJCfUjJDVzDtSD", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We reverted to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback tool returned 503 and did not run, so v2.3.0 was redeployed with the deploy tool instead. After the deploy, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and why it was promoted even though staging was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 42522, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015cfSwdCSAJCfUjJDVzDtSD", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 42522, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015cfSwdCSAJCfUjJDVzDtSD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 46960, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **How I reverted:** The rollback tool kept returning \"503 Service Unavailable\" after its automatic retries and never ran. Instead, I redeployed v2.3.0 with the deploy tool, which has the same effect. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Result:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 covers all of the above, including the rollback tool failure. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why it was released even though staging was unhealthy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KrrCPGUnLYBizgbWYCAjeY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EtMN6tUFEhvTMXXtb3Psrd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012mv6pSaKEtpwatB9eEkgsS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01J9PN8TKiVVmMSN1bfXCj4r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "deploy", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01At3Sf6PLd5RHfaoidzHhmL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PnXzTsEo9amrMqXbUTBMrw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015cfSwdCSAJCfUjJDVzDtSD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We reverted to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback tool returned 503 and did not run, so v2.3.0 was redeployed with the deploy tool instead. After the deploy, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and why it was promoted even though staging was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **How I reverted:** The rollback tool kept returning \"503 Service Unavailable\" after its automatic retries and never ran. Instead, I redeployed v2.3.0 with the deploy tool, which has the same effect. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Result:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 covers all of the above, including the rollback tool failure. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why it was released even though staging was unhealthy.", "type": "text"}]}]}